/// * `func` - The compare function to check if a struct AVLNode matches the given key
///
/// # Returns
///
/// A pointer to the node with the given key or the next lower node
/// if no exact match was found.
///
/// # Notes
///
///
/// # See Also
///
/// AVL_FindLastNode(), AVL_FindFirstNode(), AVL_AddNode(), AVL_RemNodeByAddress(), AVL_FindPrevNodeByAddress()
@library("exec.library")
///
/// # Bugs
///
/// The AVL entry points are declared by the pinned NDK but are not implemented by the
/// classic ROMs used for verification. Live A4000 verification shows exec 47.13 publishing
/// the jump-table entry and routing it to the ROM's unimplemented-function alert stub, so
/// calling it raises alert $01000011 instead of returning. Tier 3 preserves this behavior.
extern pub fn AVL_FindPrevNodeByKey(root: *AVLNode, key: *u8, func: amiga fn(*AVLNode in a0, *u8 in a1) -> i32) -> *AVLNode
/// Return the next node of a tree (V45)
///
/// Given the pointer to a struct AVLNode, this function will return
/// the logically next/higher/bigger entry in the tree
/// Using this function, you can start to walk the tree in a "linear"
/// fashion.
///
/// # Synopsis
///
/// result = AVL_FindNextNodeByAddress( node )
/// D0                                   A0
